## Key patterns

### Idempotency (cron)

Every cron handler verifies it produces the same result when run twice:

```typescript
it('does not send reminder twice', async () => {
  await handleSendReminders(req, env);  // sends
  const r2 = await handleSendReminders(req, env);  // skips
  expect(r2.data.sent).toBe(0);
  expect(r2.data.skipped).toBe(1);
});
```

### Environment isolation (repositories)

```typescript
it('dev rows invisible to production queries', async () => {
  await insertEnquiry({ ...data, environment: 'development' }, devEnv);
  const result = await getEnquiryByEmail(data.email, prodEnv);
  expect(result).toBeNull();
});
```

### Error class mapping (security)

```typescript
it('never exposes internal error details', async () => {
  const res = handleApiError(new Error('DB password abc123'));
  const body = await res.json();
  expect(body.error).toBe('Internal server error');
  expect(JSON.stringify(body)).not.toContain('abc123');
});
```

## Running tests

```bash
npm test                           # run all 231 tests
npx vitest run --reporter=verbose  # show every test name

# Full quality check before commit:
npm test && npm run lint && npx tsc --noEmit
```

